# Build artefacts
node_modules/
coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# dist/ is INTENTIONALLY committed - the official hljs grammar
# template does the same (see highlightjs/highlightjs-grammar-template
# .gitignore which only ignores node_modules). The reasoning:
#   1. npm publish ships dist/ via package.json `files: ["src", "dist"]`
#   2. CDN URLs like https://unpkg.com/highlightjs-typst/dist/typst.js
#      only resolve if dist/ is in the published tarball
#   3. The committed dist/ is exactly what the markup tests
#      run against in CI - no risk of "tests pass, publish fails"
# Regenerate with `npm run build` after any source change
# and commit the resulting dist/ updates in the same PR.

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.tsbuildinfo
